Original commit body from 2c6032fdd8fdbee52891bad4739d9bffb6a9460b:

Same-day amendment, after the owner asked whether ADR-0057 extends past
Rust. The model did; the plan did not, in two places I put there:

1. The merge key in §3 as first filed was Rust-shaped ("last `::` segment,
   SCIP token inside tree-sitter item"). §10 now requires every backend to
   DECLARE its merge anchor — languages, a name_key normaliser, a span_role
   of token|item, authoritative_for (measured, cited), and ADR-0045 §5's
   executes_analysed_code, which is also not yet implemented (no such field
   in core). register_analyzer already takes backend and languages; neither
   Rust registration sets either, so the registry cannot tell they are two
   backends for one language. The pass refuses an undeclared producer by
   name rather than falling through; unknown declaration keys raise.

2. §5's "until a per-attribute measurement shows otherwise" had no
   measurer — the measurement was a scratchpad script. §10 makes it
   load-bearing: no default exception and no authority declaration without
   a committed docs/audits/ table produced by the backend-agreement
   instrument.

§11: on an edge, src, dst and edge_type are identity, not attributes; a
disagreement is two edges, each with its origin. This is why the SCIP
edge-type row is a prerequisite, and it settles external targets for the
next backend (two stubs merge iff their canonical external identity
matches).

§12: cross-backend tests import recorded producer-shaped fixtures with the
producer version pinned; a lint refuses a test that builds the alternative
arm's input from the incumbent's output (the INV-dolud failure mode).

Consequences and Tracker items updated; CHANGELOG and the ADR index row
extended.

Tracker: four rows filed and sequenced — WI-hohuh (producer contract) and
WI-romuh (fixtures) block WI-kokiz; WI-givib (cache key folds in the resolved
backend set, split from WI-gojum sub-component 3) blocks WI-dajif
(backend-agreement instrument), which blocks WI-hukuf. WI-kokiz's
description re-scoped to read the declaration. Note on WI-gojum.

